hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3051","Narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad az-Za'farani, narrated to us Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah, narrated to us al-'Ala' ibn al-Musayyib, on the authority of Abu Umamah at-Taymi who said:\n\nI said to Ibn 'Umar: \We are a people who rent out our mounts for this journey (Hajj)"," and indeed my people claim that we do not have Hajj (valid Hajj).\""\n\nIbn 'Umar said: \""Do you not circumambulate the House (the Ka'bah)? Do you not run between as-Safa and al-Marwah? Do you not... do you not...?\""\n\nIndeed"," a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him the same as you asked me"," and he did not know what to reply until this verse was revealed:\n\n*\""There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord.\""* [Qur'an 2:198]\n\nSo he called the man and recited it to him"," then said: *\""You are pilgrims (Hajjaj).\""*\n\nNarrated to us 'Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Masruq al-Kindi"," narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Za'idah"," on the authority of al-'Ala' ibn al-Musayyib.\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"3052","Narrated to us by al-Zu'farānī, who said: Narrated to us Asbāt ibn Muḥammad al-Qurashī, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr al-Fuqaymī—though I absolve myself of any guarantee regarding his transmission—from Abū Umāmah al-Tamīmī, who said: I said to Ibn ʿUmar something to the same effect.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
